/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-_RUN-260810-634751.log:2003:.spec/decisions.md-22-| ADR-018 | Accepted | Pin Sparkle 2.9.4 exactly in `ReluxProxyMac`; require EdDSA-signed payloads plus a signed appcast with pre-extraction verification and no failure expiry; publish only final Developer ID-signed, hardened-runtime, notarized/stapled DMGs; use default stable plus opt-in `prerelease` items on the public HTTPS feed; replace/activate the direct-distribution packet-tunnel system extension only after host relaunch; use higher-build forward rollback because Sparkle 2 has no downgrade path; iOS stays with the App Store |
/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-_RUN-260810-634751.log:2009:.spec/decisions.md-28-| ADR-023 | Accepted | Scope the M0 SSH transport contract to **viability** (Option A). M0-viability-mandatory: pre-auth raw host-key evidence, approved public-key authentication, `direct-tcpip`, bidirectional exec plus exec/stdin relay upload, client-initiated rekey by byte/time threshold, bounded buffers and backpressure, deterministic cancellation and lifecycle, keepalive, privacy-safe errors, and cheaply-available metrics. Deferred to M3 as explicitly evidence-gated obligations, never silent waivers: (1) consumer-driven receive-window credit with an immutable per-channel cap, (2) the RFC 4254 channel-open rejection reason taxonomy, (3) exact exec-exit metadata distinguishing `status(0)` from `notReported` and exposing `coreDumped`, (4) deep rekey and keepalive observability including server-initiated KEX lifecycle/generation and reply-correlated keepalive RTT/timeout/miss. M0 adapters MUST surface deferred semantics as explicit not-reported/unsupported states. Owner tasks: `TASK-260728-yx2fca` (contract re-scope), `TASK-260728-3cveay` (M3 delivery). Resolves the three-round `TASK-260715-1ozsb6` stop-the-line. |
/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-_RUN-260810-634751.log:2012:.spec/decisions.md-31-| ADR-026 | Accepted | **Sparkle key generation is separated from updater integration.** The EdDSA keypair is generated and taken into custody at the up-front ceremony `TASK-260728-q5kjta`, because it depends on nothing; `TASK-260717-ziprhs` records the resulting public-key/custody evidence unattended. `SUPublicEDKey` pinning, CI signing-secret binding, and appcast sign/verify evidence are a distinct downstream task (`TASK-260728-3bj9bk`) blocked by the generated macOS target (`TASK-260715-uyju7n` → `TASK-260717-xempiv`) and the appcast pipeline (`TASK-260717-1mt4e7`). An accepted key ceremony never implies a working self-update signing path. |
