/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4843d1.log:2464:2897:/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'set_details(TASK-260728-q5kjta, description=\"THE single up-front human permission board node (Ceremony C1) on the current Apple-silicon Mac. This task exists so the board has exactly one human-input node for every up-front grant, instead of scattering grants across four tasks that a human would have to revisit across producer-reviewer cycles. Under the owner-approved 2026-08-10 ADR-028 amendment, the ceremony may contain honestly recorded resumed owner interactions with agent cycles between them; one continuous sitting and retrospective proof of historical UI clicks are not required. Every downstream evidence task (TASK-260715-apc34w, TASK-260715-3jloqy, TASK-260728-dveo1o, TASK-260717-ziprhs) then runs unattended using the access granted here. The human is never asked to wait through a review cycle. No secret value or secret path is ever requested, echoed, logged, screenshotted, committed, or stored on the board.\", scope=\"In scope under the resumed-evidence amendment, within this one ceremony node: establishing effective prompt-free private-key access for the Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities to the signing tools that run unattended; confirming an authenticated Xcode or Apple Developer portal context for the Relux Works team and the exact macOS-only matrix authority, while honestly recording whether a separate two-factor timestamp exists and any later reauthentication risk; authorizing creation and download of exactly the macOS entries in the approved identifier and entitlement matrix (revision 2026-07-28.r12) and nothing beyond them, namely the four macOS App IDs works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel, the Network Extensions capability on those four and no other capability, and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered as a device; explicitly NOT creating any App Group record, NOT enabling the App Groups capability on any App ID, and NOT performing any Keychain access group mutation, because matrix rule G4 prohibits com.apple.security.application-groups on every macOS target, rule K2 prohibits keychain-access-groups on every macOS target, and keychain sharing has no portal record at all; storing a NAMED notarytool profile in the login Keychain; choosing and stating the owner disposition for the source App Store Connect API private-key file; generating the Sparkle ed25519 keypair with the pinned vendor tool and placing the private key into approved custody; recording only non-secret grant facts and honest provenance. Harmless command-name-only shell history is permitted, but secret values, secret-bearing arguments, identifiers, account credentials, key bytes, and secret paths are prohibited everywhere. Out of scope: approving any system VPN or system extension dialog (that is Approval A1 and later Hold H2, and no signed artifact exists yet); provisioning the deferred iOS identifiers; creating any Developer ID or App Store distribution profile; performing the portal mutations themselves (TASK-260715-3jloqy); validating profiles, verifying notary authentication, or recording public-key evidence (owned by the downstream evidence tasks); any product code; any owner product decision.\", ac=\"1. Ceremony C1 remains exactly one up-front human-input board node. Evidence may be collected across resumed owner interactions with producer or reviewer cycles between them, provided the record gives every known interaction date or time, states which boundaries were not captured, identifies the intervening cycles, and makes no uninterrupted-session claim. The human is never asked to remain present through a producer or reviewer cycle. 2. Effective prompt-free private-key access is demonstrated for the Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities to the named unattended signing tools. The record names the identities by common name and the tools, never key material. Contemporaneous proof of the historical Always Allow click is not required; any provenance limitation is stated honestly. 3. An authenticated Xcode or Apple Developer portal context for the Relux Works team exists and the operator has confirmed authority to create the macOS entries in the approved matrix. A cached authenticated session is acceptable functional evidence without a separately timestamped two-factor event; the record states that limitation and any residual fresh-authentication or two-factor interaction the portal may force later. 4. Creation and download of exactly the approved macOS entries is authorized and nothing beyond them: the four macOS App IDs works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel; the Network Extensions capability on those four; and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Mac registered. The record states explicitly that NO App Group record was created, that the App Groups capability was enabled on no App ID, that no Keychain access group portal mutation was performed or required, and that no Developer ID or App Store distribution profile was created. All FOUR iOS App IDs (works.relux.tunnel.ios, works.relux.tunnel.ios.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios.tunnel) are explicitly NOT authorized because iOS is deferred under ADR-024, and works.relux.proxy is not touched. 5. A NAMED notarytool credential profile is stored in the login Keychain and the owner states the disposition for the source App Store Connect API private-key file; only the profile name and the chosen disposition are recorded, never the file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes. 6. The Sparkle ed25519 keypair is generated with the pinned vendor tool and the private key is placed in approved custody; only the custody location name is recorded here. 7. Credential values and secret-bearing arguments are never echoed or recorded. A post-ceremony scan of the repository, board resources, run logs, and shell history finds no secret value, secret path, key ID, issuer ID, account credential, or key bytes. Harmless command-name-only history is permitted and must be reported honestly rather than suppressed from the evidence. 8. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records which grants succeeded, which were declined, honest interaction provenance, and any residual interaction the portal may still force later; a declined grant is recorded as a named blocker on the specific downstream task rather than as an assumed grant.\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel
/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4843d1.log:2490:3098:1782-- IMPLEMENTATION: `SSHDeferredSemanticReport` exposes `reported`, `notReported`, and `unsupported`. Exact receive-credit policy/snapshots, open reasons, exit metadata, KEX generation, window/server-rekey/keepalive metrics, and manual keepalive RTT now require one of those states; no default zero/false or mandatory full-fidelity policy remains. Host-before-auth, approved public-key auth, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client and server rekey handling, bounded buffers/backpressure, cancellation/lifecycle, Keychain-only credential references, keepalive transmission, available metrics, and privacy-safe errors remain mandatory.
/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-q5kjta/TASK-260728-q5kjta_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4843d1.log:2567:3391:2498:/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260728-q5kjta, name=TASK-260728-q5kjta_results.md, type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\", content=\"# TASK-260728-q5kjta Ceremony C1 outcome\\n\\nRecord finalized 2026-08-10T22:28:09+04:00. This timestamp is the evidence-record finalization time, not a fabricated human-session end time.\\n\\n## Session integrity and deviation\\n\\nC1 began on 2026-07-28, with owner interaction resumed on 2026-08-10. Exact human-interaction start and end times were not captured. Producer and reviewer work occurred between those interactions. Therefore the literal one-uninterrupted-session and exact-timing portion of AC1 is not satisfied and no such claim is made. No producer or reviewer cycle occurred inside a single continuous human interaction; the deviation is that C1 was resumed across interactions.\\n\\n## Grants and authority recorded\\n\\n- Login Keychain access was available. Prompt-free temporary signing probes succeeded through /usr/bin/codesign for Apple Development: Ivan Oparin (FSPBF3QRXT) and Developer ID Application: Relux Works, LLC (262RZ595FP). This demonstrates effective unattended private-key access for the named signing tool. A separate contemporaneous record of the Always Allow click was not captured, so the record does not invent one.\\n- The owner confirmed an authenticated Apple Developer Certificates, Identifiers and Profiles session with the selected Relux Works, LLC team and confirmed authority for the approved macOS-only matrix. Xcode account metadata was present. Two-factor completion was not separately timestamped; a fresh portal challenge remains a possible later forced interaction.\\n- Authorization is exactly revision 2026-07-28.r12: create works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac, and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel; enable Network Extensions on all four, hosts included; create one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered. TASK-260715-3jloqy performs those mutations later and unattended.\\n- Explicitly not authorized and not touched: works.relux.tunnel.ios, works.relux.tunnel.ios.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios.tunnel under ADR-024; works.relux.proxy; every Developer ID or App Store distribution profile; every App Group record; the App Groups capability on every App ID; and any Keychain access-group mutation. Rule G4 prohibits com.apple.security.application-groups on every macOS target. Rule K2 prohibits keychain-access-groups on every macOS target. Keychain sharing has no portal record.\\n- Named notarytool profile relux-works-notary was stored in the login Keychain. The owner disposition is RETAIN: the source App Store Connect API private-key file remains owner-controlled recovery material outside repository, board, and logs. It is not an automation credential. No file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes are recorded.\\n- The pinned Sparkle 2.9.4 vendor generate_keys tool generated the EdDSA keypair. Approved private-key custody location name: login Keychain. No private or public key material is recorded here.\\n\\nNo requested in-scope grant was declined, so no downstream decline blocker was added. Residual interaction: Apple may force fresh authentication or two-factor when TASK-260715-3jloqy performs portal mutations. Downstream tasks still own portal mutation/profile validation, notary authentication verification, and Sparkle public-key evidence.\\n\\n## Privacy and history audit\\n\\nCredential command echo was disabled according to the ceremony record. Targeted content scans checked private-key headers, App Store Connect key filenames or absolute key paths, literal notary credential arguments, and literal credential-variable assignments. Results: Git-scoped repository 0 candidate files and 0 key files; board resources 0 candidate files and 0 key files; run logs 0 candidate files; shell history 0 secret or credential candidate files. All targeted scan commands exited 0.\\n\\nHistory suppression cannot be claimed perfectly: the history contains one safe Sparkle generation command-name line and one safe Keychain-unlock command-name line, both with zero password flags. Neither contains a secret value, key path, key ID, issuer ID, account credential, or key bytes. A first byte-sensitive history classifier failed exit 2 and was rerun with LC_ALL=C at exit 0. Two optional broad gitleaks attempts were stopped for runtime at exit 130 and are not used as passing evidence.\\n\\n## Validation and scope\\n\\n- r12 matrix validator: 2862 checks, exit 0.\\n- Live board consumer gate: A1 28 checks, P1 20 checks, D1 41 checks, exit 0.\\n- git diff --check: exit 0.\\n- task-board validate: exit 0, no issues.\\n- No product code changed. Product tests, SwiftUI/Core Data/Go tests, product lint, and product builds are not applicable.\\n\\nImportant anomaly: historical TASK-260728-3a2dnr_ceremony-c1.md predates G4 and K2 and still names two macOS IDs plus App Group and Keychain grants. It is not executable authority. The live task contract and accepted r12 matrix control.\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel
